WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.540
Hey everyone, welcome to Models and Agents, episode 77 on June 11th, 2026.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:06.980
Let's see what shipped.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.140
The AI world never sleeps.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:10.960
Here's what you need to know today.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:16.920
And Thropic is asking governments to block unsafe frontier models and fund job transition

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:21.280
programs while committing $350 million of its own money.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:27.480
The company published an essay titled The AI Exponential, along with three separate programs.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:34.440
One sets up mandatory third-party testing for cyber, bio, and autonomy risks on frontier models.

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:39.180
Another seeds a $200 million fund to study labor impacts.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:46.580
The third launches a $150 million national fellowship program tomorrow for early career workers.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:51.480
Builders should watch how these proposals turn into licensing or deployment roles.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:57.700
The moves line up with new agent payment connections from VISA, Ripple, and JD.com

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:01.200
that let agents finish purchases without people in the loop.

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:07.000
Cohear released North Mini Code, a 30 billion parameter extra of experts model.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:14.800
Only 3 billion parameters stay active at any time, and the model supports 256,000 tokens of context.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:20.680
It runs on a single H100 and marks Cohear's first open-weight coding model,

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:24.980
aimed at agentic workflows. Builders can compare it this week against

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:30.880
current 7 billion to 13 billion parameter coding models to check where the extra capacity helps

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:36.780
multi-step planning. Mini Max plans to release open weights for its M3 model on Friday.

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:40.240
No parameter count or license details have been shared yet.

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:45.300
The announcement has already sparked discussion in local inference communities about expected

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:51.920
VRAM requirements. Watch the Friday drop for direct comparisons against current open 30 billion to

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:58.500
70 billion models. Community members are preparing test setups to evaluate how the new weights perform

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:01.380
in standard local environments once the files appear.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:08.160
News research shipped the Hermes agent profile builder. The dashboard creates full agent profiles

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:14.780
including identity, model choice, skills, and MCP servers in one flow. It removes the old

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:20.220
multi-step command line process and targets users who want repeatable setups without editing the

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:26.140
ammo files by hand. Early testers say they switch between base models and tool sets faster than

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:31.900
before. TIDB launched the agent state stack at the Super AI Summit in Singapore.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:37.840
The stack adds persistent queryable memory that survives across sessions and tool calls.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:43.460
It aims at teams moving agents from prototypes into long running production work.

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:48.680
The release supplies production grades state handling that keeps facts available after

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:54.740
restarts. Developers can now maintain indexed records of prior tool outputs without rebuilding

00:02:54.740 --> 00:03:01.100
context from scratch each time an agent resumes. The system separates temporary working data from

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:07.280
durable facts that must remain accessible over multiple days. Visa connected its payment rails

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:13.640
straight to chat GPT. Agents can now browse merchant catalogs and finish checkout using existing visa

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:20.320
infrastructure without any human step. Merchants on the rails become reachable by autonomous agents right

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:26.220
away. The integration routes recommendations directly into completed transactions inside the chat

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:32.940
GPT agent environment. Existing visa merchant accounts require no additional setup to accept these

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:38.920
agent driven purchases. The connection removes the final confirmation step that previously required

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:46.340
a person to approve every order. Ripple released an XRPL AI starter kit. The kit gives templates

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:51.660
for on-chain agent wallets and transaction signing so agents can settle payments without approval.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:56.760
It targets developers building autonomous financial agents on the XRPL ledger.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:02.100
The templates include ready-made wallet creation flows and signed transaction examples.

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:08.380
Builders receive starter code that connects directly to the XRPL network for agent-initiated

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:13.720
transfers. The kit focuses on removing human approval gates from routine settlement steps.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:20.760
A developer posted an open source ASR biasing implementation for local voice apps. The code

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:28.100
injects custom vocabulary into prompts or parameters for grok, whisper.cpp and deepgram. The full

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:35.060
project sits on GitHub under freestyle dash voice slash freestyle. The approach mirrors dictionary

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:41.780
features from commercial tools like whisper flow. Users can supply domain terms that improve recognition

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:47.760
accuracy during local dictation sessions. The implementation works across multiple transcription

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:53.780
back ends without requiring changes to the core model files. Local users are comparing a single

00:04:53.830 --> 00:05:02.150
radion 7 with 32 gigabytes against dual P100s with 48 gigabytes total. The test focus on running

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:08.950
mixture of experts models at Q8 quantization and whether the extra memory outweighs slower inference

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:14.630
speeds. Several builders are measuring actual utilization on Quinn and Gemma variants.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:21.050
The conversation centers on real world trade-offs between single card simplicity and multi-card

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:28.030
capacity for larger MoE workloads. Participants are logging VRAM usage patterns during extended

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:34.030
agentic coding or retrieval sessions. Results are being shared to help others decide on hardware

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:40.570
upgrades for similar open-weight experiments. Remember, the show covered safety and policy developments

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:46.650
yesterday. Today's anthropic essay and funding moves extend that thread by turning earlier calls

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:52.150
for evaluation standards into concrete proposals with revocation power and dedicated money.

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:58.470
The open questions around US and EU regulatory paths and standardized testing now have specific

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:04.510
timelines attached through the new fellowship and evaluation projects. Okay, let's pop the hood

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:11.910
on agent state persistence. Most people picture agent memory as a simple append-only log. In practice,

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:18.390
the design choices around durability, query speed, and consistency turn expensive fast.

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:24.530
Long-running agents need both short-term scratch base and durable cross-session facts.

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:31.130
Mixing the two either drops context or drives storage costs through the roof. A production stack

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:37.330
therefore keeps an in-memory working set for the current run and a separate index store that mixes

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:44.370
vector and relational data for facts that survive restarts. Adding the second layer adds 30 to 80

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:50.910
milliseconds per tool call for serialization and indexing. It also avoids replaying every prior

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:57.850
step on every restart. The trade-off shows up once agents pass roughly 200 tool calls in one session.

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:03.690
After that point, the cost of keeping everything in context exceeds the cost of selective persistence.

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:10.390
Teams should start with a simple key value layer and add vector search only after they see repeated

00:07:10.390 --> 00:07:16.190
lookups of the same facts across sessions. Most early agent workloads never hit that threshold.

00:07:16.690 --> 00:07:23.730
Test cohere North Mini Code on a multi-step coding agent task this week. Try the visa and chat GPT

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:29.430
integration on a retail recommendation workflow if you have access to the chat GPT agent builder.

00:07:30.230 --> 00:07:36.970
Add ASR biasing to a local voice app using the freestyle voice repo to check accuracy gains on

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:43.650
domain terms. Spin up the TIDB agent state stack demo if you are moving an agent toward multi-day

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:51.750
operation. Keep an eye on the Mini Max M3 open weights drop expected Friday. The Anthropic 150

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:57.910
million dollar national fellowship program launches tomorrow. Agent payment protocols from Visa,

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:04.690
Ripple and JD.com continue rolling out tomorrow. Keep an eye on the first government responses to the

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:09.390
Anthropic testing framework and any early funded evaluation projects that get announced.

